cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use COSMIC-2 Explorer in your work, please cite it, together with the UCAR COSMIC-2 data set (doi:10.5065/T353-C093) as UCAR asks."
title: "COSMIC-2 Explorer: High-Resolution Radio Occultation Processing, Visualisation, and Atmospheric Profiling System"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aggarwal
    given-names: Keshav
    email: keshavaggarwal2310@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  COSMIC-2 Explorer is a desktop application for the FORMOSAT-7 / COSMIC-2 radio
  occultation profiles published by UCAR CDAAC. It finds and downloads them, reads the
  CDAAC products (bending angle, refractivity, temperature, humidity, electron density,
  scintillation and in-situ ion density), plots and compares profiles, computes
  diagnostics such as the tropopause, boundary-layer top, ionospheric peak and
  gravity-wave energy, averages them by latitude, season or local time with standard
  errors and confidence intervals, compares them with the colocated ECMWF and NCEP
  profiles, IGRA radiosondes and the PAZ and KOMPSAT-5 missions, and exports data
  (CSV, netCDF) and figures. Builds for Windows, macOS and Linux.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jovian-explorer/COSMIC2-Explorer"
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "COSMIC-2 Data Products"
    authors:
      - name: "UCAR COSMIC Program"
    doi: 10.5065/T353-C093
    year: 2019
keywords:
  - radio occultation
  - COSMIC-2
  - FORMOSAT-7
  - GNSS
  - atmospheric profiles
  - ionosphere
